      "content": "interesting. i think that's going to work well for the lecture.\n\none thing though—some students might argue that the book is a bit unfair, like it's basically just a character assassination of anyone on that side of the aisle and doesn't actually represent the motivations of people who follow him. how should i handle that critique in my talk? do i need to acknowledge any validity in their arguments, or is it more effective to just stick to the idea that the book is exposing a fundamental truth?",
